# Related publications
references:
  - type: article
    title: >
      Parity Vector Analysis in the Study of the Collatz Conjecture
    authors:
      - family-names: Hikawa
        given-names: Kazunobu
        affiliation: Professor Emeritus, Kanazawa Gakuin University
        orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0004-8667-0132
      - family-names: Nakanishi
        given-names: Kazuo
        affiliation: Professor Emeritus, Kanazawa Gakuin University
    year: 2026
    month: 1
    url: https://doi.org/10.13140/RG.2.2.12065.06240
    doi: 10.13140/RG.2.2.12065.06240
    notes: >
      Preprint available at ResearchGate, January 2026.
      This is the preceding work in which the counting identity
      X(d+1) = W(d) was first discovered algorithmically.

  - type: article
    title: >
      Finite-Dimensional Combinatorial and Arithmetic Structures of Parity Vectors for the Accelerated Collatz Map
    authors:
      - family-names: Hikawa
        given-names: Kazunobu
        affiliation: Professor Emeritus, Kanazawa Gakuin University
        orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0004-8667-0132
    year: 2026
    month: 7
    url: https://doi.org/10.13140/RG.2.2.29894.84804
    doi: 10.13140/RG.2.2.29894.84804
    notes: >
      Preprint available at ResearchGate, July 2026.
      The paper proves the structural identity X(d+1)=W(d) through an explicit bijection, establishes a 2-adic rigidity theorem within fixed (k,d) layers, and develops a geometric interpretation on the (k,d) lattice plane.
